@startuml gold-status-ran-detail
!pragma layout smetana
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName DejaVu Sans
title Gold-status в RAN: что реально учитывает scheduler

rectangle "Policy context from core" as POL {
  rectangle "Gold data profile\nhigher AMBR\nQCI/5QI 6/8/custom\nhigher ARP" as GOLD
  rectangle "Default data profile\nQCI/5QI 9\nbest effort\nlower ARP" as DEF
  rectangle "Voice profile\nQCI/5QI 1 + GBR/GFBR\nQCI/5QI 5 signaling" as VOICE
}
node "eNodeB/gNB" as RAN {
  rectangle "Admission Control\nGBR budget, ARP,\ncell load" as ADM
  rectangle "DRB/QoS queues\nvoice, gold data,\ndefault data" as QUE
  rectangle "QoS-aware Scheduler\npriority, weight,\nfairness, CQI/SINR" as SCH
  rectangle "Radio resources\nPRB, slots,\nMIMO layers, beams" as RES
}
actor "Gold UE" as GUE
actor "Default UE" as DUE
actor "Voice UE" as VUE

GOLD --> ADM
DEF --> ADM
VOICE --> ADM
ADM --> QUE
QUE --> SCH
SCH --> RES
RES --> GUE : more chance of PRB\nunder congestion
RES --> DUE : elastic throughput\nslows first
RES --> VUE : low-delay protected\nvoice resources

note bottom of SCH
Gold-status повышает вероятность ресурса,
но не создает радиоемкость. UE с плохим SINR
может потребовать больше PRB на тот же bitrate.
Строгая гарантия требует GBR/GFBR + admission control.
end note
@enduml
